1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means warszawsky, the copyright holder named above.

"Software" means the Licensor's original work known as No More Stupid Buys,
first published at github.com/warszawsky/no-more-stupid-buyes, in every
version, including versions published before this License was added: its
source code, browser extension, build files and tests, the duck artwork and
images generated from it, other assets and documentation, and contributions
accepted under clause 4.5. It includes any copy or portion of that work in
any form, including in modified versions, forks, compiled builds and
installers, to the extent protected by copyright or any other right. It
excludes Third-Party Components.

"Third-Party Components" means material included with or used by the
Software that others make available under their own license terms, such as
Electron (including the Chromium, Node.js, FFmpeg and other code it
contains), installer and runtime code added by build tools such as
electron-builder and NSIS, and npm packages such as ws, get-windows and
@mapbox/node-pre-gyp, together with their dependencies.

"person" means an individual or an organisation. "organisation" means any
legal person, entity or arrangement other than an individual, incorporated
or not, including a partnership, trust, foundation, state, public body or
state-owned enterprise. "you" means any person who uses, copies, modifies,
distributes or otherwise deals with the Software, whether or not that person
has rights under this License.

"Restricted Territory" means the territory of the Russian Federation and of
the Republic of Belarus within their internationally recognised borders, and
any other territory that either of them administers, except any part of
Ukraine (see UN General Assembly resolutions 68/262 and ES-11/4), Georgia or
the Republic of Moldova within their internationally recognised borders,
including any part of those countries occupied by the Russian Federation.
"Occupied Ukraine" means any territory of Ukraine temporarily occupied by
the Russian Federation.

"Restricted Person" means:
  (a) an individual who is ordinarily resident in the Restricted Territory,
      or who is physically present there other than in transit (including
      while leaving Occupied Ukraine), but not an individual who is detained
      or held captive there, or who was deported or forcibly transferred
      there from Ukraine or another territory occupied by the Russian
      Federation;
  (b) an organisation incorporated in, or having its registered office,
      headquarters, central administration, place of effective management
      or principal place of business in, the Restricted Territory;
  (c) the Russian Federation and the Republic of Belarus, including their
      state, regional and municipal bodies, agencies, armed forces, National
      Guard, and security, intelligence and law-enforcement services,
      wherever located; any body of the Union State of Russia and Belarus;
      and any state corporation or state company of either;
  (d) any authority, administration or other body established, installed
      or controlled by the Russian Federation or the Republic of Belarus in
      any territory outside the Restricted Territory that either of them
      occupies, effectively controls or claims to have annexed, including
      Occupied Ukraine;
  (e) an individual serving in, or under contract with, the armed forces,
      National Guard or any other armed, paramilitary or volunteer
      formation, private military company, or security, intelligence or
      law-enforcement service of or acting for the Russian Federation or
      the Republic of Belarus, while so serving, except an individual
      ordinarily resident in Occupied Ukraine who is compelled to serve;
  (f) an organisation, wherever established, in which one or more persons
      described in (b) to (f), or individuals described in (a) because they
      are ordinarily resident in the Restricted Territory, hold,
      individually or in aggregate, directly or indirectly (including
      through nominees, trusts or other arrangements), 50 percent or more
      of the shares, capital, voting rights or rights to profits, or which
      any of them otherwise controls, directly or indirectly (through
      ownership, voting rights, the power to appoint or remove its
      management, contract or otherwise); and
  (g) any person, to the extent acting on behalf of or at the direction of,
      or using the Software in performing work or providing services for, a
      person described in (a) to (f).

No individual is a Restricted Person merely because of their citizenship,
passport, nationality, ethnic origin, language or place of birth. Living in
Occupied Ukraine does not by itself make an individual a Restricted Person,
and being registered under Russian law while located there does not by
itself make an organisation one. However, an individual who moved to
Occupied Ukraine after 20 February 2014, having been ordinarily resident in
the Restricted Territory immediately before, is treated as ordinarily
resident in the Restricted Territory unless they had earlier been ordinarily
resident in Ukraine; and an organisation that after that date moved its
registered office, headquarters, management or principal place of business
from the Restricted Territory to Occupied Ukraine is treated as not having
moved it.

Physical presence is a question of fact at the time of the act concerned; a
VPN, proxy, remote access, or a foreign account, address, telephone number
or payment method does not change it. An individual is ordinarily resident
where they actually have their main home, whatever their registered address
or residence registration; an individual who moves out of the Restricted
Territory to live elsewhere stops being ordinarily resident there when they
move.


