3. RUSSIA AND BELARUS RESTRICTION

3.1 No rights for Restricted Persons or in the Restricted Territory. A
person has no rights under this License while, and to the extent that, they
are a Restricted Person. No rights are granted for anything done in the
Restricted Territory, by anyone, except personal use (including installing
and copying for that use) by an individual who is not a Restricted Person.
No one may exercise rights under this License through, for, or in providing
work or services to, a Restricted Person, and a person's rights do not
extend to its employees, officers, contractors, agents or affiliates who are
Restricted Persons, even when they act for it. A person who stops being a
Restricted Person has the rights in Section 2 from then on, including in
copies they already hold, unless those rights were terminated under clause
3.4; nothing done while they were a Restricted Person becomes licensed.

3.2 No supply to Restricted Persons. It is a condition of this License that
you do not sell, distribute or otherwise make the Software available
(including over a network), directly or indirectly, to any person you know,
or have reasonable grounds to believe, is a Restricted Person, will pass it
to one, or will use it in the Restricted Territory beyond what clause 3.1
allows. Publishing the Software openly with this License included does not
by itself breach this clause, provided that:
  (i) the publication is not directed at Restricted Persons (using the
      Russian, Belarusian or Ukrainian language does not by itself make it
      so);
  (ii) it is not made on or through a platform, store, mirror, registry or
      other service operated by a Restricted Person or from the Restricted
      Territory, or intended mainly for users there (for example RuStore,
      GitFlic, GitVerse or SourceCraft); uploading the Software to such a
      service is making it available to a Restricted Person; and
  (iii) where the service offers any means of excluding countries or
      regions, you use it to exclude the Restricted Territory.
A failure to meet (iii) alone is treated as a breach of clause 3.3, not of
this clause.

3.3 Keeping the terms. If you distribute the Software or any substantial
portion of it, in original or modified form, you must include this License
with its text unchanged (in source form, as a LICENSE file at the top level
of the Software; in builds, installers and packaged extensions, as a file
packaged with them). You may add your own copyright notices and license
terms for your own modifications next to this License, but not inside it.
Any terms under which you distribute the Software must be subject to
Section 3, and any Software distributed with your modifications remains
subject to this License. You must not state, including in package metadata
or license identifiers, that the Software or any work containing it is
licensed under the MIT License or any other license that lacks Section 3.
Anyone who receives the Software, from any source, receives this License,
subject to clause 3.1, directly from the Licensor and each contributor, and
no one can grant broader rights in the Software.

3.4 Consequences. Anything done with the Software by a person while they
are a Restricted Person, or excluded by clause 3.1, is outside the scope of
this License, and any license or sublicense purportedly granted to a
Restricted Person has no effect. Any distribution in breach of clause 3.2
is outside the scope of this License and was never licensed, and it
terminates all your rights under this License automatically and
immediately, without notice, unless the Licensor reinstates them in
writing. If you breach clause 3.3 (but not clause 3.2), your rights
terminate unless you cure every such breach within 30 days after you first
become aware of it or are notified of it by the Licensor, whichever is
earlier; a timely cure counts as if the breach had not occurred, and
otherwise only the Licensor can reinstate your rights, in writing. Persons
who are not Restricted Persons and who received the Software from you keep
their rights as long as they comply with this License. The Licensor retains
all rights and remedies under applicable law.


